usage: flair isoalleles [-h] --isoform_bed ISOFORM_BED -g GENOME --bam BAM
                        --read_map READ_MAP --phased_vcf PHASED_VCF
                        [--germline_vcf GERMLINE_VCF]
                        [--sample_name SAMPLE_NAME] [--normal_bam NORMAL_BAM]
                        [--normal_read_map NORMAL_READ_MAP]
                        [--normal_name NORMAL_NAME]
                        [--tumor_vcf TUMOR_VCF | --somatic_vcf SOMATIC_VCF | --variant VARIANT]
                        [--min_normal_depth MIN_NORMAL_DEPTH]
                        [--carrier_min CARRIER_MIN] [--min_tagged MIN_TAGGED]
                        [-o OUTPUT] [-t THREADS] [--generate_map]
                        [--label_bams] [--temp_dir TEMP_DIR]

Each isoform's reads by haplotype, and in a tumor and normal pair by somatic
variants, with the sequence and protein of each, from reads haplotagged by a
phasing tool (such as WhatsHap) and the read map of flair quantify. One
sample: --bam, --read_map and --phased_vcf. A pair adds --normal_bam and
--normal_read_map, --phased_vcf being the normal's, and one way of choosing
the somatic variants: --tumor_vcf, --somatic_vcf or --variant

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --germline_vcf GERMLINE_VCF
                        the germline variant calls, of the sample, or in a
                        pair the normal, when --phased_vcf holds only some of
                        them, as when only hets were phased: every passing
                        call is a germline variant, phased by --phased_vcf.
                        bgzipped and indexed (default: --phased_vcf)
  --sample_name SAMPLE_NAME
                        the name of --bam's sample in the outputs (default:
                        its file name)
  --carrier_min CARRIER_MIN
                        an unphased germline het is put on the haplotype
                        holding at least this share of an isoform's tagged
                        reads carrying it (default: 0.9)
  --min_tagged MIN_TAGGED
                        the tagged reads carrying an unphased germline het
                        needed to place it (default: 10)
  -o OUTPUT, --output OUTPUT
                        output file name base (default: flair)
  -t THREADS, --threads THREADS
                        batches of genes processed at once (default: 4)
  --generate_map        write each sample's reads by isoform and group,
                        <output>.isoalleles.<sample>.read.map.tsv
  --label_bams          write each sample's assigned reads with their isoform
                        and group in the IA tag,
                        <output>.isoalleles.<sample>.bam (in IGV, group by tag
                        IA)
  --temp_dir TEMP_DIR   directory for temporary files, in a directory of the
                        run's own (default: $TMPDIR)

required named arguments:
  --isoform_bed ISOFORM_BED
                        the isoforms, the flair isoform bed the read maps were
                        made with by flair quantify; its CDS gives each
                        isoform's start codon. Fusion isoforms are left out
  -g GENOME, --genome GENOME
                        FASTA of the genome, indexed with samtools faidx
  --bam BAM             the sample's (in a pair, the tumor's) reads aligned to
                        the genome, sorted and indexed, haplotagged (HP and PS
                        tags) by the phasing of --phased_vcf
  --read_map READ_MAP   the read map flair quantify --generate_map wrote for
                        --bam's sample, <output>.<sample>.read.map.tsv, plain,
                        bgzip or gzip
  --phased_vcf PHASED_VCF
                        the germline variants, phased: the VCF the phasing
                        tool wrote and haplotagged --bam with, the sample's
                        own, or in a pair the normal's. bgzipped and indexed

tumor and normal pair:
  --normal_bam NORMAL_BAM
                        the normal's reads, haplotagged by the same phasing as
                        --bam; makes the run a pair, whose tumor reads, of
                        --bam, are grouped by somatic variants too
  --normal_read_map NORMAL_READ_MAP
                        the read map of --normal_bam's sample, from the same
                        flair quantify
  --normal_name NORMAL_NAME
                        the name of the normal in the outputs (default: its
                        file name)
  --tumor_vcf TUMOR_VCF
                        the tumor's variant calls: its passing calls that
                        --phased_vcf, the normal's, does not call are somatic
                        if at least --min_normal_depth normal reads inform the
                        site, and are otherwise left out, in excluded.tsv.
                        bgzipped and indexed
  --somatic_vcf SOMATIC_VCF
                        the somatic variants, every passing call of a somatic
                        caller's VCF (such as ClairS or DeepSomatic), as it
                        calls them. bgzipped and indexed
  --variant VARIANT     a somatic variant, CHROM:POS:REF>ALT, or CHROM:POS for
                        every alt the VCFs have there; may be given more than
                        once. Only the variants given are somatic, whatever
                        the VCFs call, as for a known driver the normal calls
                        because tumor cells are in it
  --min_normal_depth MIN_NORMAL_DEPTH
                        with --tumor_vcf, the normal reads informing a site
                        for a tumor-only call there to be somatic (default:
                        10)
